<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Adaptive launcher foreground. It is the app mark (vault_app_icon) inset so the
  whole shield stays inside the icon's visible region: launchers mask, shift and
  zoom the 108dp foreground layer, and only the central 72dp of it is guaranteed
  to be shown (66dp is the documented safe zone).

  vault_app_icon is cropped tightly to the shield (243.89 x 304.23 units, aspect
  0.8017), so it is portrait and has no transparent margin to rely on. The insets
  below build an inner box with that same aspect ratio, so the shield fills the box
  exactly at its previous on-screen size:

    inner height = 108 - 2 * 27.24 = 53.52dp
    inner width  = 108 - 2 * 32.55 = 42.90dp   (42.90 / 53.52 = 0.8017)

  The shield is therefore ~53.5dp tall and ~42.9dp wide and centred in the layer,
  unchanged from before the crop (its farthest corner stays ~34.3dp from the
  centre, as it did when the shield sat inside the padded 432dp asset). Per-side
  dimensions are used instead of a uniform inset so the box can be non-square and
  match the asset's aspect ratio.
-->
<inset xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:drawable="@drawable/vault_app_icon"
    android:insetLeft="32.55dp"
    android:insetTop="27.24dp"
    android:insetRight="32.55dp"
    android:insetBottom="27.24dp" />
